    "strategy_summary": "Execute auto/exports cluster first (22 dead barrel re-exports). Then barrel-hygiene for remaining barrel cleanup. Then output-structural-debt to fix import cycle. Then stale-docs, code-cleanup, param-sprawl, type-narrowing, error-gaps for review issue fixes. Finally, re-review 7 stale subjective dimensions after mechanical cleanup is complete.",
    "trigger": "manual_triage",
    "last_completed_at": "2026-03-22T06:23:08+00:00",
    "last_triage": {
      "completed_at": "2026-03-22T06:23:08+00:00",
      "stages": {
        "observe": {
          "stage": "observe",
          "report": "## Observe Stage: Mechanical Backlog Verification\n\nNo open review issues to verify (all 17 previously resolved). 181 mechanical items in backlog across 3 auto-clusters and 146 unclustered items.\n\n### Security cluster (2 items) \u2014 ALL FALSE POSITIVES\n\n- hash: security::src/settings/repo-settings/diff.ts::security::hardcoded_secret_name::src/settings/repo-settings/diff.ts::40\n  verdict: false-positive\n  verdict_reasoning: Variable 'secretScanning' is a key in PROPERTY_MAPPING that maps camelCase config names to GitHub API snake_case field names ('_secret_scanning'). The underscore prefix is an intentional marker for special handling (line 66 checks startsWith('_')). Not a hardcoded credential.\n  files_read: [src/settings/repo-settings/diff.ts]\n  recommendation: Skip as false-positive\n\n- hash: security::src/settings/repo-settings/diff.ts::security::hardcoded_secret_name::src/settings/repo-settings/diff.ts::41\n  verdict: false-positive\n  verdict_reasoning: Variable 'secretScanningPushProtection' maps to '_secret_scanning_push_protection' \u2014 same API field mapping pattern as above. Not a secret.\n  files_read: [src/settings/repo-settings/diff.ts]\n  recommendation: Skip as false-positive\n\n### Import cycle (1 item) \u2014 NEEDS INVESTIGATION\n\n- hash: cycles::src/output/sync-report.ts::src/output/sync-report.ts::src/output/unified-summary.ts\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: unified-summary.ts imports renderSyncLines from sync-report.ts (line 5). sync-report.ts does NOT import from unified-summary.ts based on grep. However, desloppify detected a cycle \u2014 may involve transitive or type-level imports not visible in simple grep. Worth investigating deeper.\n  files_read: [src/output/sync-report.ts, src/output/unified-summary.ts]\n  recommendation: Investigate whether this is a transitive cycle through barrel files\n\n### Dead exports cluster (22 items) \u2014 GENUINE BUT NEED CARE\n\nVerified that barrel files re-export types nobody imports from the barrel:\n- src/vcs/index.ts exports CommitOptions, CommitResult, MergeOptions, MergeResult, PRStrategyOptions, CloseExistingPROptions, INetworkGitOps \u2014 all used internally via direct imports from types.ts, and by tests importing from types.ts directly. Nobody imports these from the barrel.\n- src/vcs/index.ts exports IGitOps, ILocalGitOps, FileAction, GitAuthOptions, GitOpsOptions \u2014 these ARE imported from the barrel by src/sync/types.ts and other consumers. They are USED.\n- src/sync/index.ts exports DiffStats, computeUnifiedDiff, isBinaryFile \u2014 need verification\n- src/config/index.ts exports ContentValue \u2014 imported by src/sync/file-writer.ts from config/index.ts, so USED\n- src/settings/index.ts exports SettingsAction \u2014 need verification\n- src/shared/gh-api-utils.ts exports ResolveGitHubTokenOptions \u2014 need verification\n- src/vcs/authenticated-git-ops.ts exports AuthenticatedGitOpsOptions \u2014 test file has unused import of this type\n\nCaution: CLAUDE.md warns \"NEVER remove exports without checking test imports.\" Tests import some of these from types.ts directly, not from barrels. Safe to clean barrel re-exports but must verify each one individually.\n\n### Code smells (64 items) \u2014 MIXED\n\nHigh cyclomatic complexity findings (normalizer.ts 6x, settings-report.ts 3x, validator.ts 2x, etc.) are genuine but these are validation/normalization functions where branching is inherent. Not-worth-it to refactor most \u2014 complexity is essential, not accidental.\n\n- hash: smells::src/vcs/pr-creator.ts::async_no_await\n  verdict: not-worth-it\n  verdict_reasoning: createPR() and mergePR() are async functions that return promises from async operations without await. This is valid \u2014 returning a promise directly from an async function is idiomatic. The async keyword is correct because callers expect Promise<T>.\n  files_read: [src/vcs/pr-creator.ts]\n  recommendation: Skip \u2014 valid pattern\n\n- hash: smells::src/cli/program.ts::console_error_no_throw\n  verdict: not-worth-it\n  verdict_reasoning: CLI entry point catches fatal errors, logs via console.error, and exits with process.exit(1). This is the correct CLI error handling pattern. Throwing from a .catch() handler would be worse.\n  files_read: [src/cli/program.ts]\n  recommendation: Skip \u2014 correct CLI pattern\n\n- hash: unused::test/unit/authenticated-git-ops.test.ts::AuthenticatedGitOpsOptions:6\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Line 6 imports ILocalGitOps from types.js. The test file does not import AuthenticatedGitOpsOptions anywhere. The import of ILocalGitOps may or may not be used \u2014 should verify and remove if unused.\n  files_read: [test/unit/authenticated-git-ops.test.ts]\n  recommendation: Check if ILocalGitOps is used in the test, remove if not\n\n### Boilerplate duplication (10+ items) \u2014 GENUINE\n\nMultiple boilerplate blocks repeated across output module files (github-summary.ts, lifecycle-report.ts, settings-report.ts, sync-report.ts, unified-summary.ts). These are report-rendering functions with shared patterns that could be extracted into helpers.\n\n### Test coverage (11 items) and test health (71 items in test/unit)\n\nTest health items are primarily in test files \u2014 likely test-specific smells that need individual assessment.\n\n### Summary\n\nPriority order for execution:\n1. Security false positives \u2014 skip immediately (2 items, quick win for strict score)\n2. Dead exports \u2014 clean up barrel files (genuine, ~10-15 items worth fixing)\n3. Unused test import \u2014 quick fix (1 item)\n4. Boilerplate duplication \u2014 extract shared helpers (medium effort, good score impact)\n5. Cyclomatic complexity \u2014 selective refactoring where possible\n6. Stale subjective dimensions \u2014 need re-review (7 dimensions stale)",
          "cited_ids": [],
          "timestamp": "2026-03-22T06:11:27+00:00",
          "issue_count": 0,
          "dimension_names": [],
